f Nod (sorry, had to)<br /> <br /> <b>Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised,Transylvania Chronicles I: Dark Tides Rising</b><br /> Kupala's sacred fire-flower<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</b><br /> Guarded Rubrics (not an artifact perse, but a whole ancient library entrusted to the Tal'mahe'Ra by the being called Inauhaten)\u200b<br /> <br /> So far I can't find anything about\u200b the <b>Spear of Bathel</b>...<br /> But the hunt is on!<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for this! It's certainly going to make it easier to look for them, I didn't even remember the &quot;Road books&quot; had relics in them! Yesterday I looked for the <b>Spear of Bathel</b> in the Encyclopedia Vampirica, but couldn't find it. But the list is certainly going to be very helpful for this story I'm concocting! A thousand thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T10:44:12-07:00","id":1510214,"title":"","content":"Well, I couldn't find anything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think - tho' I could be wrong - the <b>Spear of Bathel</b>\u200b was a BJD thing<br /> Will continnue to search, I have a hunch IF it ever were mentioned it wasn't in a Vampire supplement, more like a Hunter or Inquisitor or Mage thing<br /> <br /> The reason I think this is because what I found regarding Bathel:<br /> <br /> The holy site of Bethel played an important role in the lives of Abraham and Jacob/Israel, as well as in later Israelite history. Abraham built an altar between Bethel and Ai <b>(Genesis 12:8)</b>, and Jacob, en route to Haran while fleeing from Esau, experienced a vivid dream at Bethel <b>(28:10-17)</b>. Before moving on, he set up a commemorative stone at the spot. In addition to serving as places of remembrance, such stones occasionally marked burial sites (<b>35:20</b>).<br /> Biblical scholars have long debated Bethel\u2019s precise location. Most have placed it at modern Tell Beitin, 13 km north of Jerusalem, but El Bireh, a few km farther south, has also been suggested. Clearly Bethel was located within the area north of Jerusalem now referred to as the West Bank.<br /> Tell Beitin, which shows signs of occupation beginning with the Chalcolithic period, was continuously occupied during the Middle Bronze Age I and II, until the city was destroyed around 1550 B.C. A late Bronze Age city located on the same site, dating from the fourteenth century B.C., boasted high-quality houses, streets with flagstone pavements, and sewers. There is evidence of its destruction at the end of the Bronze Age, and a later, Iron Age I settlement at the location reflects an impoverished community. This city continued to exist through the Iron Age, but no remains of Jeroboam\u2019s temple \u2013 which the Babylonian army destroyed in 586 B.C. \u2013 have been found here.<br /> According to Onomasticon, written by Eusebius (A.D. 269-339) and revised by Jerome (A.D. 345-419), Bethel was located at the twelfth Roman milestone on the eastern side of the road leading north to Neapolis (called Shechem in the Old Testament; modern Nablus). In this ancient manuscript Tell Beitin is described as being located at the fourteenth milestone, indicating that, if Eusebius\u2019 information was correct, it could not have been Bethel. Bethel may, then, have been situated a little to the south , at modern El Bireh, near the city om Ramallah. No excavation has been done at El Bireh, a town currently occupied by Palestinians.<br /> During the period of Israel\u2019s monarchy, Bethel (\u201cHouse of God\u201d) came to be embroiled in a controversy. Associations with its sacred history and monuments led the people to transform it into a centre of idolatrous worship.<br /> Jeroboam I, for example, took advantage of the holy traditions associated with Bethel and, against God\u2019s will, set up a shrine there to serve as an alternative worship site to Solomon\u2019s temple (<b>1 Kings 12:26-30</b>). As a result the prophets sverely censured worship at Bethel. Hosea (<b>Hosea 4:15, 5:8, 10:5</b>) went so far as to refer to Bethel as Beth Aven, a disparaging pun meaning \u201chouse of wickedness\u201d. Such texts indicate that there was a debate during ancient times over whether Bethel was a sacred site or a centre of apostasy.<br /> The name Bethel was at the centre of debate in another context. Bethel appears as a god\u2019s name in a seventh-century B.C. Assyrian treaty and in some texts from Elephantine, located in southern Egypt. Based upon these discoveries, some scholars have argued that the word Bethel is used in the Old Testament as a divine name rather than as a place-name. Most interpreters remain unconvinced of the validity of this theory, since it appears quite evident that the Biblical Bethel was a specific place. In fact, certain Biblical texts seem to attest that Bethel in its early days was a city formerly known as Luz (mentioned in <b>Genesis 28:19, 35:6, 48:3</b>) but renamed by Jacob (<b>Judges 1:23</b>).\u200b<br /> <br /> In this light, it is a bit understandable why a spear from Behtel would be a relic that shields the wielder from damage, while slaying any foe it even scratches... <br /> But how it ended up in the posession of Siegfried, the Ventrue Prince of Vancouver, a Visigoth chieftain who born in 356 CE and Embraced 378 CE and achieved legendary fame when he signed the Covenant, a peace treaty between the local Kindred and the Lupines (In exchange for aiding in reforestation attempts and fighting against resource exploitation, the Lupines would guard his domain from any unwanted intruders and would refrain from unprovoked violence against vampires under Siegfried's protection. Siegfried's rule was so secure that he managed to abolish most traditional positions of power within a domain, holding all power by himself)?<br /> Good question... <br /> But Siegfried also dealt with mages from the Syndicate (not knowing that they were corrupted by the Wyrm and cooperating with Pentex)<br /> Not to mention, before the Covenant, Siegfried was saved from Final Death at the claws of Lupines by Marcus Vitel, promising a Life Boon in return (Vitel would claim this boon half a century later, selecting to embrace Misery, who, until that night, was to be the prince's childe. Despite this, she was still schooled as a Ventrue, until Vitel returned to claim her after her training was done)<br /> The Covenant broke around the late 1990s, when the Glass Walker representative Roger Daly was murdered and a casino was built over a dormant Pit that set several Banes free...<br /> Lets not forget, many powerful princes owe favors to Siegfried. The peace that he has kept in Vancouver, between the clans and with the Garou, has impressed even the most powerful of the Camarilla. He has a high status among all vampires and clans.<br /> It is not hard to explain how such relic ended up in his posession... <br /> <br /> But what that relic actually is? <br /> Let's hope we will find something<br /> But it is totally in the realm of possibility, BJD just &quot;inveted it&quot; and we are on a wild goose chase <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T09:02:18-07:00","id":1510367,"title":"","content":"I think we shouldn't assume that it's a relic from V:tM. World of Darkness inhabitants sometimes interact with each other so maybe it's a Fetish, mage Talisman, maybe even fae Treasure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T20:08:13-07:00","id":1510459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510160-spear-of-bathel?p=1510214#post1510214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I couldn't find anything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think - tho' I could be wrong - the <b>Spear of Bathel</b>\u200b was a BJD thing<br /> Will continnue to search, I have a hunch IF it ever were mentioned it wasn't in a Vampire supplement, more like a Hunter or Inquisitor or Mage thing<br /> <br /> The reason I think this is because what I found regarding Bathel:<br /> <br /> The holy site of Bethel played an important role in the lives of Abraham and Jacob/Israel, as well as in later Israelite history. Abraham built an altar between Bethel and Ai <b>(Genesis 12:8)</b>, and Jacob, en route to Haran while fleeing from Esau, experienced a vivid dream at Bethel <b>(28:10-17)</b>. Before moving on, he set up a commemorative stone at the spot. In addition to serving as places of remembrance, such stones occasionally marked burial sites (<b>35:20</b>).<br /> Biblical scholars have long debated Bethel\u2019s precise location. Most have placed it at modern Tell Beitin, 13 km north of Jerusalem, but El Bireh, a few km farther south, has also been suggested. Clearly Bethel was located within the area north of Jerusalem now referred to as the West Bank.<br /> Tell Beitin, which shows signs of occupation beginning with the Chalcolithic period, was continuously occupied during the Middle Bronze Age I and II, until the city was destroyed around 1550 B.C. A late Bronze Age city located on the same site, dating from the fourteenth century B.C., boasted high-quality houses, streets with flagstone pavements, and sewers. There is evidence of its destruction at the end of the Bronze Age, and a later, Iron Age I settlement at the location reflects an impoverished community. This city continued to exist through the Iron Age, but no remains of Jeroboam\u2019s temple \u2013 which the Babylonian army destroyed in 586 B.C. \u2013 have been found here.<br /> According to Onomasticon, written by Eusebius (A.D. 269-339) and revised by Jerome (A.D. 345-419), Bethel was located at the twelfth Roman milestone on the eastern side of the road leading north to Neapolis (called Shechem in the Old Testament; modern Nablus). In this ancient manuscript Tell Beitin is described as being located at the fourteenth milestone, indicating that, if Eusebius\u2019 information was correct, it could not have been Bethel. Bethel may, then, have been situated a little to the south , at modern El Bireh, near the city om Ramallah. No excavation has been done at El Bireh, a town currently occupied by Palestinians.<br /> During the period of Israel\u2019s monarchy, Bethel (\u201cHouse of God\u201d) came to be embroiled in a controversy. Associations with its sacred history and monuments led the people to transform it into a centre of idolatrous worship.<br /> Jeroboam I, for example, took advantage of the holy traditions associated with Bethel and, against God\u2019s will, set up a shrine there to serve as an alternative worship site to Solomon\u2019s temple (<b>1 Kings 12:26-30</b>). As a result the prophets sverely censured worship at Bethel. Hosea (<b>Hosea 4:15, 5:8, 10:5</b>) went so far as to refer to Bethel as Beth Aven, a disparaging pun meaning \u201chouse of wickedness\u201d. Such texts indicate that there was a debate during ancient times over whether Bethel was a sacred site or a centre of apostasy.<br /> The name Bethel was at the centre of debate in another context. Bethel appears as a god\u2019s name in a seventh-century B.C. Assyrian treaty and in some texts from Elephantine, located in southern Egypt. Based upon these discoveries, some scholars have argued that the word Bethel is used in the Old Testament as a divine name rather than as a place-name. Most interpreters remain unconvinced of the validity of this theory, since it appears quite evident that the Biblical Bethel was a specific place. In fact, certain Biblical texts seem to attest that Bethel in its early days was a city formerly known as Luz (mentioned in <b>Genesis 28:19, 35:6, 48:3</b>) but renamed by Jacob (<b>Judges 1:23</b>).\u200b<br /> <br /> In this light, it is a bit understandable why a spear from Behtel would be a relic that shields the wielder from damage, while slaying any foe it even scratches...<br /> But how it ended up in the posession of Siegfried, the Ventrue Prince of Vancouver, a Visigoth chieftain who born in 356 CE and Embraced 378 CE and achieved legendary fame when he signed the Covenant, a peace treaty between the local Kindred and the Lupines (In exchange for aiding in reforestation attempts and fighting against resource exploitation, the Lupines would guard his domain from any unwanted intruders and would refrain from unprovoked violence against vampires under Siegfried's protection. Siegfried's rule was so secure that he managed to abolish most traditional positions of power within a domain, holding all power by himself)?<br /> Good question...<br /> But Siegfried also dealt with mages from the Syndicate (not knowing that they were corrupted by the Wyrm and cooperating with Pentex)<br /> Not to mention, before the Covenant, Siegfried was saved from Final Death at the claws of Lupines by Marcus Vitel, promising a Life Boon in return (Vitel would claim this boon half a century later, selecting to embrace Misery, who, until that night, was to be the prince's childe. Despite this, she was still schooled as a Ventrue, until Vitel returned to claim her after her training was done)<br /> The Covenant broke around the late 1990s, when the Glass Walker representative Roger Daly was murdered and a casino was built over a dormant Pit that set several Banes free...<br /> Lets not forget, many powerful princes owe favors to Siegfried. The peace that he has kept in Vancouver, between the clans and with the Garou, has impressed even the most powerful of the Camarilla. He has a high status among all vampires and clans.<br /> It is not hard to explain how such relic ended up in his posession...<br /> <br /> But what that relic actually is?<br /> Let's hope we will find something<br /> But it is totally in the realm of possibility, BJD just &quot;inveted it&quot; and we are on a wild goose chase <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! That was an amazing research my friend. I found it fascinating that the word Bethel could be a &quot;god's name&quot;, I would never have any idea about it and also of note is the discussions regarding the real meaning behind the name. <br /> <br /> Siegfried is indeed a notorious Cainite that managed to do something few Cainites have ever done and I particularly like the character a lot. It's always interesting to go outside the norm regarding a Princedom and they made it a good job to make his domain feel very unique. Some of my players became fan of the scenario when I presented it to them, they even wanted to leave the Camarilla behind to stay in the city. I'm not familiar with this story regarding his relationship with Vitel and especially Misery, could you tell me the source? Is in the new materials for V5?<br /> <br /> Again, thank you very much for the amazing research, I also fear it's going to be hard to find much information about the Relic itself. I might give the wearer some defence bonus, or perhaps do something similar to the Excalibur's Scabbard, that protects the wearer from any damage that would result in bleeding, i.e. most physical attacks. On the other hand, I'm not sure it's a good idea to make it identical to another already existing relic (if I'm not mistaken the Excalibur's Scabbard is from Changeling, my memory sometimes betrays me these days lol, but I guess it happens with anyone who read too much). And regarding damage, I want to avoid opting for the &quot;easy route&quot; of making it cause double damage, I'm still hopeful we're going to find more information about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T20:10:47-07:00","id":1510460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510160-spear-of-bathel?p=1510367#post1510367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we shouldn't assume that it's a relic from V:tM. World of Darkness inhabitants sometimes interact with each other so maybe it's a Fetish, mage Talisman, maybe even fae Treasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it's another idea to look for the information in other supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T22:48:39-07:00","id":1510465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510160-spear-of-bathel?p=1510459#post1510459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with this story regarding his relationship with Vitel and especially Misery, could you tell me the source? Is in the new materials for V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is from <b>Children of the Blood </b>from Misery's bio","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T08:21:30-07:00","id":1510491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510160-spear-of-bathel?p=1510465#post1510465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is from <b>Children of the Blood </b>from Misery's bio</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https: